# Function-like macros, #, ## and __VA_ARGS__ (approach.md, "ccpp
# design", step 5). Lines 1-6 define F (id 34; its parameters a 35,
# b 36), B (37), S (38; x 39), CAT (40), V (41; __VA_ARGS__ 42, f 43)
# and G (44).
43 54 4b 04     # "CTK", version 4
02 07 00        # up to line 7: 6 lines, so a jump
# line 7: F(1, x) is 1 + x * 2
05 01 00 2b 04 27 00 2a 05 02 00
01
# line 8: B(B(1)): the argument is expanded first, so [ [ 1 ] ]
5b 5b 05 01 00 5d 5d
# line 9: S(a  +  "b\n") is a string: a + "b\n", 9 bytes, the blanks
# made one space each. A string is held until the token after it, whose
# line it takes (line 10), so both next-line codes come first.
01 01
08 09 61 20 2b 20 22 62 5c 6e 22
# line 10: x1 (a new id, 43), +=, and y (44): an empty left operand
04 2d 00 ca 04 2e 00
01
# line 11: f(1, 2) and f()
04 2b 00 28 05 01 00 2c 05 02 00 29
04 2b 00 28 29
01
# line 12: G is F, which then takes (3, 4) from the line: 3 + 4 * 2;
# the last F has no '(', so it stays a name
05 03 00 2b 05 04 00 2a 05 02 00
04 22 00 3b
01              # the end is on line 13
00 2e 00 ss ss  # the end: 46 ids, the checksum
